      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hardware security keys provide phishing resistance because they validate the origin site cryptographically, unlike SMS codes which can be hijacked via SIM-swapping. These keys rely on public-key cryptography, meaning the secret key never leaves the physical device, preventing remote extraction attempts. This architectural difference makes them impervious to credential stuffing and Man-in-the-Middle attacks that plague SMS-based authentication.",
